  "text": "Answer the following question based on the information given below.\n In a sport event, six teams (A, B, C, D, E and F) are competing against each other. Matches are scheduled in two stages. Each\n team plays three matches in Stage-I and two matches in Stage-II. No team plays against the same team more than once in the\n event. No ties are permitted in any of the matches. The observations after the completion of Stage-I and Stage-II are as given\n below.\n Stage-I:\n   One team won all the three matches.\n   Two teams lost all the matches.\n   D lost to A but won against C and F.\n   E lost to B but won against C and F.\n   B lost at least one match.\n   F did not play against the top team of Stage-I.\n Stage-II:\n   The leader of Stage-I lost the next two matches.\n   Of the two teams at the bottom after Stage-I, one team won both matches, while the other lost both matches.\n   One more team lost both matches in Stage-II.\n The only team(s) that won both the matches in Stage-II is (are)\n A. B   B. E & F   C. A, E & F   D. B, E & F   E. B & F",
  "key": null,
